.venv/
# No data in git. Keep only the directory skeleton, so a fresh clone has
# somewhere to put it -- git will not descend into an excluded directory, so the
# directories must be re-included before their .gitkeep files can match.
data/**
!data/**/
!**/.gitkeep

# ...EXCEPT the scoreboard, which is a REFERENCE and not an output.
#
# Every calibration figure in this repository is quoted as "the committed
# data/processed/history.json". It was never committed. It is overwritten by
# every run, so nothing could diff it, no test could compare a document against
# it, and three separate reviews rediscovered the same class of staleness --
# ranks 4-12 written up as n=26 / PIT 0.750 / 46% four minutes after the file on
# disk said n=28 / 0.757 / 43%. A reference artefact that cannot be diffed is
# not a reference.
#
# history.json is the machine-readable one and is what
# tests/test_calibration_report.py checks the documents against. history.md is
# tracked with it because it is the human-readable rendering of the same run and
# a diff of the two together shows what moved and what it means. Both are
# written by src/compare_history.py with json.dumps(indent=2), so the diff is
# line-oriented and readable.
!data/processed/history.json
!data/processed/history.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# agent worktrees and local claude state
.claude/
